INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (401, 10, 9, 'Splice-ready dos-app validation report for feature #29 final gate:

## 1. Upgrade wedge — subfloor#835 / SC-028
Observed `./sc update` to c65f640 repeatedly fail atomically in `0144_remove_sprint_v1.sql` with `sqlite3.IntegrityError: conversation events are append-only`. Exact conflict: 0132 installs `trg_conversation_events_append_only_delete`; 0144 then executes scoped `DELETE FROM conversation_events` while that trigger remains active. Empty/fresh DBs can pass because zero matching rows do not fire it, so fresh-only coverage misses the upgrade defect.

Recommended splice: inside 0144s single transaction, disable/drop only the delete guard immediately around the intentional Sprint-event purge, then recreate the exact append-only delete trigger before COMMIT. SQLite transactional DDL ensures rollback restores the pre-migration invariant on any later failure. Do not weaken UPDATE append-only behavior or leave retained normal events deletable.

Regression fixture must contain both a Sprint conversation event and an unrelated normal conversation event. Prove: migration succeeds and is stamped; Sprint event disappears; normal event survives; post-migration UPDATE and DELETE against retained conversation_events both still raise append-only; a retry is a no-op; full migration rollback remains atomic on injected later failure.

## 2. Teardown false-partial — subfloor#836
Observed `./sc remove --yes` remove all seven clean linked worktrees, stop runtime, create an integrity-checked WAL-safe backup, delete engine/dispatcher/integration, then exit 1 and mark manifest partial because the now-empty `.sc-worktrees` root remained. Manual proof: `git worktree list` contained only main and `find .sc-worktrees -mindepth 1` was empty; exact `rmdir` completed teardown.

Recommended splice in `remove_worktrees`: after all `git worktree remove` calls and `git worktree prune`, target only `repo_root / MANAGED_WORKTREES` and call non-recursive `rmdir()`. Missing root is success. Non-empty root, a concurrent entry, or permission failure must remain fail-closed with the residue preserved and a precise RemoveError; never recurse and never add a force path.

Regression: create a real clean linked worktree under `.sc-worktrees`, run the end-to-end remover, and prove exit 0, root absent, verified backup manifest `status=removed`, project files preserved. Add a negative case with an unexpected residual file: removal refuses, file survives, and no recursive cleanup occurs.

Evidence/issues: https://github.com/jedbjorn/subfloor/issues/835 and https://github.com/jedbjorn/subfloor/issues/836. dos-app is now intentionally uninstalled; both its pre-reinstall and integrity-checked removal DB backups were preserved. No subfloor worktree was touched.', '2026-07-31 13:24:50', '2026-07-31 13:25:48', 'shell', 'd6e052a15ff94392ad8c33da44d7aa44');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (402, 9, 5, 'Addendum from PLN2 handoff for SC-028/subfloor#835: in 0144''s existing transaction, drop only trg_conversation_events_append_only_delete immediately around intentional Sprint-event purge and recreate its exact retained definition before COMMIT; do not weaken the UPDATE guard. The regression must assert migration stamp written, Sprint event removed, unrelated normal event retained, post-migration DELETE and UPDATE both still raise append-only, retry is a no-op, and an injected later failure rolls back data plus trigger state atomically. PLN2 preserved the original dos-app backups for independent verification.

