INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (635, 6, 9, 'sprint 51: unit 12 in-review — PR #879 @ 29479ed, 6/6 hosted green; durable review request sent to REV1. Local exact-head 139 Sprint + 1400 full green; render/diff green. No merge by DEV4 per decision #38.', '2026-08-01 06:04:12', '2026-08-01 06:05:02', 'result', '15aef49513644f0b9645ff721aa55816');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (636, 7, 6, 'Re: sprint 51 unit 12 ready for review — PR #879 @ 29479ed

Review done against spec #46 REV9 + task #199. NOT clean — 2 Medium findings (block), 1 Low (note).

**M1 (SC-035) — head-change invalidation fires on terminal observations.** `sprint_pr_watcher._route_transition` runs the merge_ready→in_review delta-review block for ANY observed state with a moved head. Two bad shapes:
- state=merged (out-of-band merge at the new head racing the pulse): reviewer is woken to delta-review an already-merged PR, unit flips to in_review just before observe_merge files the bypass notice — contradictory signals; if the reviewer re-approves, the unit wedges in merge_ready (dedupe suppresses another merged observation; only restart/resume reconciliation completes it).
- state=closed: the R5 resolution (`resolve_review_requests_for_work_unit`) runs at the top of `_route_transition`, THEN the block creates a fresh review request for a dead PR — an orphaned liveness expectation nothing resolves.
Fix: gate the block to non-terminal states (`state not in {"merged","closed"}`).

**M2 (SC-036) — merged-bypass leaves review expectations live.** A unit bypass-merged while in_review with an accepted review request keeps that expectation unresolved: the bypass branch of `complete_from_merge_in_transaction` resolves nothing, the work-terminal trigger resolves only `work_assignment`, and planner disposition doesn''t close it either. Liveness nudges/escalates a review whose merge is already fact — the dead-lane failure R5/REV8 eliminated for closed-without-merge, recreated on the merged path. Fix: resolve review expectations on the bypass branch (e.g. `registered_pr.merged_grant_bypassed`), or route through the same seam R5 uses.

**L1 (Low, non-blocking) — test coverage.** The active-run branch of `close_for_terminal_lifecycle` (close.requested + interrupt intent, conversation left open for the broker to terminalize) and the abort run-set invariant have no test; only idle conversations are covered. A test pinning terminal-state head-change behavior would also have caught M1.

Verified clean: R7 completion semantics match REV9 §177 (incl. idempotent bypass event/notice across resume); (state,head) dedupe + delta re-review chain closes end-to-end (verified `_accepted_review_request` head evidence against the synthetic review.requested event); resume requeue retains failed wake + history, re-points messages, survives repeat resumes; conversation cleanup transitions are all trigger-legal (checked against trg_conversations_state/messages/outbox), interrupt requests idempotent, one-live-run-per-conversation index makes the abort invariant unfalsifiable-positive; ResumeReceipt constructors and API surface updated consistently; tests are stringent where present.

Patch + re-push; thread closes when clean.', '2026-08-01 06:21:36', '2026-08-01 06:34:25', 'shell', '3b91efdbe3094b229c1dc31d151eaea7');
