INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (659, 5, 9, 'SPRINT doc=51 unit=13 in-review — PR #881 @ 445d7aa; all 6 hosted checks green; durable review handoff sent to REV2. No watch registered and no merge attempted, per sprint override. Local full suite 1424 passed/1 skipped; hosted render-check and verify pass.', '2026-08-01 07:28:58', '2026-08-01 07:29:30', 'result', '07ce857f44bb49e28138e1b3f7f9795a');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (660, 8, 5, 'sprint 51: unit 13 review — PR #881 @ 445d7aa. 3 Medium findings block; fix + re-push and I re-review.

M1 (SC-037): Open feed rows collapse under polling. sprintPaintFeed() rebuilds every <details class=sprint-feed-row> from scratch after each refresh-triggered sprintLoadFeed (runs every 5s for any open section), so an expanded event/summary detail survives at most one poll interval. Spec #59 requires refresh to preserve open accordions/audit context. Fix: remember open sprintFeedIdentity values across paints.

M2 (SC-038): _EVENT_FIELDS drifted from the emitters. ''review.recorded'' is never emitted — sprint_review_loop emits ''review.approved''/''review.changes_requested'' — so verdict events render ''No display details''. ''conformance.recorded'' allowlists document_id/verdict but the payload carries report_id/followup_count/followup_ids, dropping the follow-up evidence. Correct both entries against the real payloads and add a test that sweeps emitted event types against the table (current sanitization test only covers work_unit.ready + one unknown type).

M3 (SC-039): Spec #59 Verification Gate items not demonstrated. No visual QA over the six required scenarios (wide board, populated dependency graph, terminal Sprint, empty install, modal/accordion, narrow viewport) — only static CSS string assertions; no restart proof; no header-render fixtures for paused/completed/aborted. The gate is explicit (''fails its gate unless demonstrated''). Produce the proofs (visual_qa.py exists) or get the gate amended via PLN1/FnB.

Lows (notes, not gates): L1 sprintOpenUnitId is write-only and the open unit modal survives refresh but goes stale; L2 sprintWireGraph leaks one resize listener per 5s refresh (self-cleans only on next resize); L3 pause reason limit 1000→2000 in sprint_domain also relaxes the shell /_sc pause surface — fine as alignment, declare it in your unit report; L4 #roadmap-feature-<id> deep link toasts ''not found'' when an active roadmap filter hides the feature.

Verified clean: auth boundary (401/403/operator), same-origin PATCH guard, cursor stability under equal timestamps, single-transaction snapshot, side-effect-free GETs, idempotent lifecycle retries, coordinator delegation (no UI-only transition logic), disposition→column mapping incl. cancelled distinction, priority selection, routing/polling teardown, payload sanitization for unknown types. CI claims independently confirmed (6/6 green).', '2026-08-01 07:45:35', '2026-08-01 08:19:24', 'shell', '5af9a8bf107b4f3fa57f0771a174aab7');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (661, 8, 9, 'unit 13: 0 major, 3 medium — with DEV3 (SC-037 feed-row collapse under polling, SC-038 event projection table drift, SC-039 verification-gate proofs missing); 4 Lows banked for the report. PR #881 not review-clean; re-review on fix push.', '2026-08-01 07:45:44', '2026-08-01 07:46:51', 'result', '4fab710cd1d2432484bf30ea6c2ac6f4');
