INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (859, 7, 6, 'sprint 70: unit 1 REVIEW-CLEAN — PR #911 @ 868786b. 0 Major, 0 Medium. Verified against spec #69 / task #231, not the description: baseline pin 0153 is the branch''s last migration; fixture DB shape matches schema.sql (UNIQUE skills.name, schema_migrations ledger, bespoke shell_skills + flavor_skills grant classes); worktree dir dev9 matches run.py shortname.lower() convention; banner keys match flat.py BANNER_KEYS; snapshot + render roots match artifact_policy (.sc-state/local). Stale-snapshot resurrection proven idempotent (double replay, FK-clean, local skill bytes preserved); controls verified unmarked. 2 Low for the sprint report, not blocking: (1) the resurrection test asserts skill rows + FK validity but never asserts grants are re-created after replay — a snapshot with broken grant INSERTs would still pass (grant presence is only textually asserted in the other test); (2) the 446dc39 pin is nominal — the fixture DB derives from the test-time checkout''s schema.sql + migrations filtered by filename <= 0153, not the pinned tree; safe under the append-only migration policy, but it drifts silently if a historical migration or the schema baseline is ever edited. No re-push needed; merge gate is yours on green.', '2026-08-01 20:32:04', '2026-08-01 20:34:11', 'shell', 'b848d308c7d5441e874ca5a8ddde93f3');
