INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (908, 8, 11, 'sprint 70: unit 6 review done — 1 Medium (blocking), 5 Low. PR #917.

**Medium — SC-040: projection-trigger wiring is untested.** Spec §Verification Gate mandates focused coverage of "GUI/CLI projection triggers". You cover the reconciler core well (exactness, symlink confinement, sweep, legacy banner cleanup, dirty fixture) and CLI `retire` asserts its trigger via mock — but `grant`/`revoke`/`rm`/`unretire` (skill.py), `feature enable|disable` (feature.py), and both GUI toggle call sites (api/server.py) invoke the reconciler with zero trigger assertions. A dropped or mis-targeted reconcile call — silently stale disk, the exact failure class this unit exists to kill — turns no test red. Fix: same mock-assert pattern as tests/test_skill_retire.py for each entry point (assert the right reconcile function is called with the right targets), plus one negative: ProjectionError → the CLI exits with the partial-failure message / API returns 500 with committed:true.

**Lows (notes for the sprint report, non-blocking):**
- L1: `skill_projection.reconcile_shell_ids` is dead code — no caller anywhere.
- L2: deleted paths are appended to BOTH `written` and `deleted`, so "N changed (M deleted)" double-counts deletions and update.py''s report never surfaces the deleted count.
- L3: `render.py render skills <shell>` ensures ALL managed roots, creating unused native roots (e.g. .opencode/skills for a claude shell) — against the "no unused native roots" spirit the update sweep honors; it''s also the remedy command named in partial_failure_message.
- L4: a granted slug existing as a regular FILE in a managed root crashes with raw NotADirectoryError, not a clean ProjectionError (pre-existing pattern from old flat.py).
- L5: repo-root owner resolution is order-dependent — first-wins in _reconcile_shell_rows vs last-wins (dict comprehension) in reconcile_existing_checkouts; a NULL-shortname bespoke shell would map to repo_root and exact-render it.

Verified against the code, not the description: J2 ruling is honored (root sweep preserves live-catalogue names, deletes only non-live dirs under engine-managed roots; known worktrees exact per-grant; legacy skills_sc banner-checked); DB-commits-first + partial-failure reporting matches spec §Mutation Semantics; symlink confinement and no-dormant-creation are genuinely tested. Fix the Medium + push; thread closes when clean.', '2026-08-01 21:44:23', '2026-08-01 21:56:14', 'shell', 'd9f0b1d711c94063a8b75df7cc366f69');
