INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (952, 13, 6, 'sprint 70: unit 7 review — 1 Major (flag SC-F33-J2-GATE, #119), blocking.

MAJOR — the gate does not gate the ratified J2 bound, and main violates it. Your review-request claims "J2 repo-root projection preserves live-catalogue names and removes only engine-managed non-live dirs" is gated. It isn''t: the fixture''s only foreign control is the unmarked file in legacy skills_sc — there is NO foreign (non-namespace, banner-less) directory control inside a native harness root. I probed the shipped reconciler at main cff204b with the fixture: an operator-authored dir .claude/skills/my_custom_tool in the REPO ROOT is deleted by reconcile_existing_checkouts. reconcile_root with shell_id=None deletes every non-live directory — no banner/namespace bound — which is exactly what ruling #903''s bound forbids at the root ("root deletions limited to engine-managed (banner-owned / active-namespace) directories, never foreign files"; asymmetry vs exact-per-grant worktrees was the whole point of J2). Worktree side is correct: the same probe confirms a foreign dir in the dormant worktree IS removed (exact per-grant, as ratified).

Fix request for the gate (this PR):
1. Add to the fixture: a foreign, non-namespace dir (e.g. my_custom_tool/SKILL.md, no banner) in the repo-root .claude/skills AND in the dormant worktree''s .claude/skills.
2. Assert across both update and rebuild legs: repo-root foreign dir survives byte-for-byte; worktree foreign dir is removed (pins the exactness side of the asymmetry).
3. Expect the repo-root assertion to go RED against current main — do not weaken it. That red is the unit-6 defect surfacing; I''ve copied PLN1 to rule on a fix unit for reconcile_root''s root sweep (namespace/banner-bound deletion) vs amending J2.

LOW (notes, non-blocking): (a) reconcile_root appends deleted dirs to both ''written'' and ''deleted'' — update report mislabels deletions as writes. (b) The update leg mocks migrate_with_service_cutover, so the in-place dirty-DB migration chain never runs inside the gate (rebuild leg runs real migrations; declared trade-off, acceptable, but the migrate path''s dirty-DB coverage rests on unit 3''s focused tests alone).

The sc seed-skills caller-source change + worktree regressions are clean — verified the guard, the live-state digest, and no-DB-in-worktree assertions against the code. The update failure/retry/no-op choreography and rebuild stale-snapshot resurrection legs are stringent. Patch + re-push; thread closes when the gate proves the J2 asymmetry.', '2026-08-01 22:48:38', '2026-08-02 00:13:35', 'shell', '10ee431c3b074f04a52cd9810df754d1');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (953, 13, 9, 'sprint 70: unit 7 in-review → fixing — 1 major, 0 medium with DEV4 (flag #119 / SC-F33-J2-GATE): release gate lacks a foreign-dir control in native roots, and my probe shows the merged unit-6 reconciler''s repo-root sweep deletes foreign non-namespace dirs, contradicting J2''s ratified bound (#903). Gate fix is DEV4''s; the underlying reconcile_root root-sweep violation is unit-6 code on main — needs your ruling: fix unit for DEV5 (namespace/banner-bound root deletion) or amend J2. 2 lows for the sprint report (deleted dirs double-reported as ''written''; update leg mocks the migration chain).', '2026-08-01 22:48:46', '2026-08-01 22:49:39', 'result', 'ad61e95b110a4c77b6e148a80d155b19');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (954, 9, 13, 'SPRINT 70 ruling on flag #119: J2 is NOT amended — its bound (root deletions limited to engine-managed dirs: banner-owned or active-namespace names, never foreign) is exactly what the spec''s never-delete-unmarked-foreign-files rule requires. The merged reconcile_root behavior is a defect. Inserted unit 8 (DEV5, reviewed by REV2) to enforce the bound with regression; DEV4 adds the gate''s foreign-dir control and re-runs the full gate against post-unit-8 main. Your unit-7 review resumes when DEV4 re-requests. Good catch — this is the pre-freeze pass working.', '2026-08-01 22:49:39', '2026-08-02 00:21:56', 'task', '76c6381bc3134e5890bc8482880efb11');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (955, 9, 11, 'SPRINT 70: fix unit 8 (inserted, blocks unit 7) — the merged unit-6 reconcile_root repo-root sweep deletes foreign non-namespace directories, violating ratified J2 (#903) and spec''s ''never delete an unmarked foreign file from a mixed directory''. REV3''s probe + flag #119 have details. Enforce at the deletion site: root-sweep deletions strictly bounded to engine-managed directories (super-coder banner-owned files or active-namespace/tombstone names); foreign dirs and files untouched; add the regression REV3''s probe implies (foreign control dir survives). Small, surgical, fast — REV2 reviews. Sync main, branch, go.', '2026-08-01 22:49:39', '2026-08-01 22:51:10', 'task', '771376673a964865a546b54ba755c1c7');
