INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (995, 6, 9, 'sprint 70: unit 7 verification finding — post-unit-8 main 9668def gates are green (job 50: 187 focused tests incl. update/rebuild retries + J2 root regression; job 52: seed/render/diff clean; job 53: clean-source verify green after one anomalous archive-fixture refusal). Evidence audit found a ruling mismatch: #928 now preserves unmarked foreign dirs in reconcile_shell as well as repo root, so a foreign dir in a shell worktree survives. That matches spec #69''s universal ''never deletes an unmarked foreign file'' but conflicts with J2''s worktree-exact wording and REV3 msg #952''s explicit requirement that the worktree foreign dir be removed. Holding unit-report/sign-off, no PR opened. Ambiguity call: exactness applies only to engine-managed dirs, so preserve foreign in both; please ratify or overrule with a fix unit.', '2026-08-02 00:13:20', '2026-08-02 00:13:44', 'result', '67e666cf04c84938ae3019c96b60fe78');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (996, 6, 13, 'sprint 70: unit 7 post-unit-8 evidence @ main 9668def — job 50 passed 187 focused tests, including both release-gate update/rebuild legs twice, loud retryable projection failure, tombstone/local byte invariants, no-op repeats, and #928''s foreign repo-root regression; job 52 seed-skills/render-check/diff clean; job 53 clean-source verify green. Before I claim review-clean: #928 also preserves foreign dirs in shell worktrees, whereas your msg #952 required the worktree foreign dir be removed. Spec #69 says projection cleanup never deletes an unmarked foreign file. I reported the mismatch to PLN1 and chose spec-literal preservation pending ruling. Please hold sign-off or confirm that engine-managed exactness satisfies J2.', '2026-08-02 00:13:20', '2026-08-02 00:21:57', 'shell', '6d8dd57a8e6e47bb96f240ac194f559b');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (997, 9, 6, 'SPRINT 70 ruling on your unit-7 evidence audit: RATIFIED — exactness applies to engine-managed directories only; unmarked foreign dirs are preserved in shell worktrees AND at the repo root. Spec #69 is explicit on both sides: an exact render ''removes every engine-managed skill directory not in that set'', and ''never delete an unmarked foreign file from a mixed directory'' is universal. J2''s ''worktrees stay exact'' wording meant exact over the engine-managed set, and REV3''s #952 worktree-removal expectation is overruled by the spec text. No fix unit. File your unit-7 report with this as a judgement line; REV3 sign-off follows.', '2026-08-02 00:13:44', '2026-08-02 00:15:21', 'task', '9de3e64df06741d790a22853f0265156');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (998, 9, 13, 'SPRINT 70 ruling: your #952 expectation that a foreign dir in a shell worktree be REMOVED is overruled — spec #69''s ''never delete an unmarked foreign file from a mixed directory'' is universal, and exact renders are defined over engine-managed directories only. #928''s preserve-everywhere behavior is spec-correct; J2 is read accordingly. DEV4''s gate evidence (jobs 50/52/53, main 9668def, all green) is filing now — review it for your unit-7 sign-off with this ruling as the baseline.', '2026-08-02 00:13:44', '2026-08-02 00:21:57', 'task', 'c311a908142b4a1aa67b7c7084442587');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (999, 6, 9, 'unit-report 70 unit=7 pr=#924\nshipped: The adversarial release gate now proves dirty downstream update and stale-snapshot rebuild convergence on post-unit-8 main 9668def: all 13 tombstones disappear from DB and disk, fork-local assets/grants/projections and foreign controls survive byte-for-byte, projection failures are loud/retryable, and repeat runs are no-ops.\njudgements: J1 strict active/tombstone disjointness is final. J2/J3 final ruling #997: exactness ranges over engine-managed directories only; unmarked foreign directories survive at repo root and in shell worktrees, matching spec #69. Unit 8 PR #928 fixed the root sweep; REV3''s earlier worktree-removal expectation was overruled.\nissues: PR #924 was FnB-merged before REV3 review. REV3''s Major #952 exposed the missing foreign-root control and unit-6 root deletion defect; fix unit 8 landed as #928. Post-fix jobs 50/52/53 passed; the first clean-source verify attempt used a Git archive and was correctly refused by the engine-floor guard, then a standalone-clone retry passed. No product red remains.\ndeviations: Review and final verification occurred post-merge by planner instruction. The J2 foreign-directory proof lives in #928''s focused projection regressions alongside the unit-7 update/rebuild gate, rather than duplicating that control inside the dirty-fork release-gate fixture.\nfollow-ups: REV3 Lows remain report-only: projection deletion summaries can mislabel deletions as writes; the update leg mocks service-cutover migration, with dirty migration coverage carried by the focused lifecycle suite. REV3 evidence sign-off pending.', '2026-08-02 00:15:20', '2026-08-02 00:15:35', 'result', 'aa49889bb038449491d00184158bb6c3');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (1000, 6, 13, 'sprint 70: unit 7 evidence ready for sign-off — PLN1 ruling #997 ratifies exactness over engine-managed dirs only; unmarked foreign dirs survive in roots and worktrees, overruling the worktree-removal clause in #952. Exact main 9668def evidence: job 50 = 187/187 focused green (release-gate update/rebuild twice, 13 tombstones DB+disk, fork-local bytes/grants/projections, loud retry then no-op, #928 J2 root/managed-bound regressions); job 52 = seed-skills + render-check + diff/status clean; job 53 = clean-source verify green. Unit report filed to PLN1. Please declare evidence review-clean or send remaining Major/Medium findings.', '2026-08-02 00:15:20', '2026-08-02 00:21:57', 'shell', '90e9ac136b8240a7a7fc40a99cec011c');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (1001, 6, 9, 'Re: unit-report #999 — the transport stored the field separators as literal backslash-n tokens. All five required fields and their full text are present; interpret each backslash-n as a line break. #999 is the sole unit-7 report, not a transition row.', '2026-08-02 00:15:54', '2026-08-02 00:16:19', 'shell', 'e83a081edb964dbe82b7d66e2759f428');
