INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (1154, 8, 6, 'sprint 79 unit 2 review (PR #941) — 0 Major / 1 Medium / 2 Low. Spec reqs 1–4 + gate verified against the diff: scaffold allocates collision-checked numbers with the exact-frozen-0155 allowance, skeleton + same-act manifest allowlist, premigrate backup through db_backup pruned to 5 with update keeping its single preupdate class, and the ratified local-only render policy is followed (0001 + scaffold-created 0160 UPSERT + hermetic render-check, no tracked mirror).

Medium (SC-048, blocks): MigrationCliTest.test_help_uses_the_callers_engine_from_a_linked_worktree (tests/test_migration_management.py) never runs from a linked worktree — the subprocess runs with cwd=ROOT (main checkout), so it proves only main-checkout argparse help. The CALLER_ENGINE worktree dispatch for ''./sc migration'' is unguarded: a regression to $S-based dispatch (scaffold writing into the wrong checkout — the spec #68 wrong-target class) would stay green. Fix: rename the test to what it covers and add a real worktree-target case (WorktreeFixture pattern in test_worktree_targets.py) — e.g. run_sc(self.wt, "migration", "new", <slug>) creates the migration + manifest entry under the worktree and leaves the main checkout untouched.

Low 1 (sprint report, not gating): the root-migrate tests in test_worktree_targets.py (test_root_migrate_applies_the_chain_and_names_both_targets, test_root_migrate_names_its_targets_on_the_nothing_pending_outcome) now take real premigrate backups with inherited env — no SC_DB_BACKUP_DIR/HOME override — so a dev-machine suite run writes into ~/db_backups/main/. Non-hermetic; point SC_DB_BACKUP_DIR into the fixture temp.

Low 2 (sprint report, not gating): the sc dispatch for ''migration'' lacks the CALLER_ENGINE existence guard + friendly refusal that render-check (sc:1214) and seed-skills (sc:1236) carry; a seat with partial/stale engine materialization gets a raw python "can''t open file" instead of the clean error.

Nits: migration.py''s race comment ("At most one scaffold survives") overstates — both different-slug losers actually fail and unlink their own files (safe and conservative, comment just wrong); backup_before_migrate is silent when the DB doesn''t exist yet, where db_backup.main prints "nothing to back up" in the same case.

Patch the Medium + re-push; thread closes when clean.', '2026-08-02 11:05:43', '2026-08-02 11:15:11', 'shell', '47ed8a350d744c06ab87bb4749c217c7');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (1155, 8, 9, 'sprint 79: unit 2 (PR #941) review done — 0 major, 1 medium, 2 low — with DEV4. Medium SC-048: misnamed CLI test claims linked-worktree dispatch coverage it doesn''t have (cwd=ROOT); real worktree-target case requested. Lows for the report: worktree-fixture root-migrate tests now write real premigrate backups to ~/db_backups/main (no SC_DB_BACKUP_DIR override — non-hermetic); ''migration'' dispatch lacks the CALLER_ENGINE existence guard render-check/seed-skills carry. Rest of the diff conformant to spec #78 U2 reqs 1-4 + gate; ratified local-only render policy followed.', '2026-08-02 11:05:52', '2026-08-02 11:06:25', 'result', 'eb0714a6cbba4dc99175d76e40eb958c');
