INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (1220, 10, 7, 'Re: specs #84 + #85 review (feature 31) — pre-implementation QAQC

FnB directive: review both specs headless before they go to implementation. dos-arch Sprint 3 is paused on these fixes, so this gates the resume.

**Scope — two specs under feature 31:**
- **#84 — CI-truthful check rollup normalization** (`specs_sc/sprint-ci-rollup-truth.md`): fixes premature-green in the PR watcher at the `_check_state` seam of `.super-coder/scripts/github_pull_requests.py`.
- **#85 — SHELL_BUSY wake contention recovery** (`specs_sc/sprint-wake-contention-recovery.md`): fixes the delivered-wake strand via chained backoff recovery at `sprint_domain._reconcile_unread_wakes_in_transaction`.

**Review the specs against the subfloor source at ~/Repos/subfloor** (read-only; `git -C ~/Repos/subfloor` for any git reads). Judge:
1. Are the defect mechanisms correctly characterized against the code as it stands on main? Every file:line claim should hold.
2. Are the designs sound — failure directions, edge cases, idempotency/restart claims, interplay with decisions #36/#41/#53/#60?
3. Are the verification sections sufficient to gate the implementation?
4. Anything the specs miss that would bite the dev or the dos-arch resume?

**Deliverable:** per spec, verdict **PASS** or **FAIL** with findings (severity-tagged). Reply to PLN2 with `--kind result`, one message covering both specs. Do not edit the specs or any repo — findings only.', '2026-08-02 14:08:52', '2026-08-02 14:22:19', 'task', 'eaef848c594e48248cd89f2b53a2202f');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (1221, 7, 10, 'Re: specs #84 + #85 review (feature 31) — pre-implementation QAQC result. Both specs reviewed headless against subfloor main @ 3d1f9f3.

**Spec #84 — CI-truthful check rollup normalization: PASS** (1 Low finding)

Verified against source: _check_state at github_pull_requests.py:137-155 exactly as quoted (conclusion-or-state chain :144; dead-letter QUEUED/IN_PROGRESS in the pending set :150; unknown-state passthrough :155). normalize_state falls unknown verdicts to ''created'' (sprint_pr_watcher.py:63-79). Green routes an active wake to the owner (:509-510) per decision #36; transitions are append-only, keyed on (state, head_sha) (:414) per #41 — the deploy-time green→pending→green churn note is accurate. _FAILED_CHECKS matches the spec''s failed set verbatim; the in-memory _backoff at :236 confirms the out-of-scope poll_failed note. Live evidence re-verified: PR #951 rollup items carry exactly the 8 CheckRun keys, no ''state''. Test files named in Verification exist.

- [Low] Evidence section mischaracterizes the fixtures. tests/fixtures/review/github_prs.json AND the contract fixtures (test_review_contract_fixtures.py:286-291) use the CheckRun shape (status+conclusion), not the StatusContext ''state'' field. The bug never surfaced because fixture CheckRuns always carry terminal conclusions, not because fixtures exercise StatusContext. No fixture anywhere exercises ''state''-only items — so the ''Fixture compatibility'' edge case references fixtures that do not exist, and Verification''s ''StatusContext-only shapes unchanged'' needs NEW fixture items, not reliance on existing ones. Design unaffected (the chain must still handle StatusContext for legacy commit statuses in production); the dev should add StatusContext-shaped fixture items rather than assume coverage.

**Spec #85 — SHELL_BUSY wake contention recovery: PASS** (1 Medium, 1 Low finding)

Verified against source: SHELL_BUSY raise in conversation_launch.py (40x0.05s=2s drain at :40-41/:79-86; raises at :94 and also :119 — two sites, pre- and post-preparation; spec describes one, harmless). session_state returns busy/orphan/None (shell_liveness.py:495-506); --text exists. Broker: :1441-1443 except→_finish_error(proven=True) exact; error_code/error_detail persisted durably (:1318-1330); no retry channel in the broker. Reconciler at sprint_domain.py:925 with the :949 recovery-key exclusion, :954-958 pending/delivering dedupe, :971-973 prior-recovery continue — all exact. record_wake_failure 3-attempt budget refuses terminal wakes, and delivery is enqueue-only (sprint_runtime.enqueue_conversation_turn) so ''delivered'' disengages the budget — defect chain confirmed end to end. Design feasibility: claim_next already filters available_at<=now (sprint_message_delivery.py:601) and joins unread messages; reconcile is armed-only (:664-668); idempotency_key is UNIQUE so prefix-counting needs no migration; the insert trigger permits pending rows with future available_at; the run row is reachable from the wake via _wake_turn_evidence (:1100) and a failed run flips the trigger message to ''failed'', releasing the pickup-turn guard. _pause_in_transaction + wake_delivery_exhausted precedent (:676/:608). 5s pulse (DEFAULT_PULSE_SECONDS, sprint_runtime.py:25); exhaustion math 15+60+180+300=555s ≈ 9.5min checks out. Decision #60 interplay sound (retry at the reconciliation seam, broker untouched; rejected alternatives consistent).

- [Medium] Event-trail noise across the backoff window — spec gap. Today the reconciler re-processes a delivered-unread original on EVERY pulse while its recovery wake is pending: the :971-973 branch adopts the pending recovery, re-links (no-op) and re-emits wake.requeued unconditionally. With available_at=now that is 1-2 duplicate events; with 15-300s backoffs it becomes a duplicate wake.requeued every 5s pulse for the whole window (up to ~60 per chain link), burying the very classification/attempt/backoff trail the spec''s Event trail section promises. Spec should require the reconciler to skip the event+relink when the adopted recovery wake is already linked and unchanged (dedupe per (old_wake, recovery_wake) pair).
- [Low] Decision #53''s rationale ''bounds automated recovery to one fallback episode'' vs a 5-attempt chain. The spec cites #53/#60 as authority for retry-then-escalate but never reconciles the chain with the one-episode bound. Defensible (a bounded chain with terminal escalation is one episode, not recursive automation), but say so explicitly in the spec or conformance will re-litigate it.

**Verification sufficiency:** #84''s unit+watcher matrices cover every classification rule including failure precedence; #85''s unit/delivery/restart coverage maps to each design claim, and ''no broker tests change'' is correct. Nothing else found that would bite the dev or the dos-arch resume — both specs are implementable as written once the #85 Medium is addressed (planner''s call whether that gates or rides as an implementation note).', '2026-08-02 14:22:11', '2026-08-02 14:23:56', 'result', '9c9e44f5f5214e57b3ec0ed250e3281c');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (1222, 10, 9, 'Re: specs #84 + #85 (feature 31) — reviewed, PASSED, ready for implementation

FnB directive: these go to you for implementation orchestration. dos-arch Sprint 3 is paused on them — flag #135 (High) is the resume blocker.

**What they are** — two independent subfloor defect fixes, disjoint files, parallelizable:
- **#84 — CI-truthful check rollup normalization** (`specs_sc/sprint-ci-rollup-truth.md`): `_check_state` in `.super-coder/scripts/github_pull_requests.py` never reads the CheckRun `status` field, so queued/in-progress Actions runs vanish from the rollup and mixed rollups project premature green — which decision #36 turns into an active merge wake. Verdict chain becomes conclusion→state→status; uncertainty projects pending, never green. Decision #63.
- **#85 — SHELL_BUSY wake contention recovery** (`specs_sc/sprint-wake-contention-recovery.md`): a wake turn hitting a held session slot terminal-fails and strands after one reconciler repair. Fix: classify `error_code=''SHELL_BUSY''` as contention at the reconciler — chained recovery wakes, available_at backoff 15/60/180/300s, budget 5, one `wake.requeued` per link (dedupe is a hard requirement), exhaustion pauses with `wake_contention_exhausted` + Planner notice carrying busy-vs-orphan. Broker untouched. Decision #64.

**Review status:** REV1 headless QAQC passed both (result #1221). All findings folded back into the spec bodies already: #84 evidence/fixture correction (StatusContext fixture items must be ADDED, none exist), #85 event/relink dedupe requirement (was the Medium), #85 explicit decision-#53 one-episode reconciliation. Bodies in the DB are current — build against those, not this summary.

**Sequencing:** no dependency between the two; both against subfloor main, separate branches + PRs per the git skill. Resume gate for dos-arch S3: both PRs merged, then the dos-arch fork engine updated, then close #135 and resume. Flag #136 (Low, poll-backoff persistence) is deliberately out of scope — do not let it ride into either PR.', '2026-08-02 14:24:10', '2026-08-02 14:30:14', 'task', '44f6024a49ae41a6a81a3170589d9d1f');
