INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (1249, 8, 5, 'sprint 86: unit 2 review of PR #958 done — 0 Major, 1 Medium, 2 Low. NOT review-clean; Medium blocks.

**Medium — SC-051 (flag #139): resume-after-exhaustion re-pause trap.** After a `wake_contention_exhausted` pause, the stranded busy recovery wake (state `delivered`, messages unread, run row durably `failed`/`SHELL_BUSY`, 4 recovery rows on the prefix) is re-scanned by `resume()`''s reconcile (`sprint_domain.py:401-406`). Classification reads the stale run row, `recovery_count` is still 4, so `current_attempt=5 >= WAKE_CONTENTION_ATTEMPTS` and the sprint re-pauses instantly (`:1011-1043`) — with a fresh planner notice every resume attempt (pause idempotency keys on version), and `resume()` returns `changed=True` though the sprint ends paused. Practical trap: the notice''s implied orphan remedy (kill the pid) does NOT unblock resume — only reading the message (GUI Retry) does, and no notice says so. Spec #85 is silent on resume-after-exhaustion (its pause/resume edge case only requires no chain growth while paused — that holds). Note the mirror of `wake_delivery_exhausted` is inexact: that path pauses on a NEW failure event; this one re-fires on durable stale evidence.
Fix direction (planner rules): (a) name the real remedy in the exhaustion notice + suppress identical re-pause notices, or (b) treat the human''s resume as the episode reset — re-deliver the stranded wake (pending, available_at=now) as the human-sanctioned retry, consistent with decision #53 (the human acted). I lean (b), but it''s a design call.

**Low 1 — dedupe verification formally vacuous.** In `test_shell_busy_retries_durably_then_pauses_with_one_notice`, the `duplicate-pulse` reconcile scans zero rows (the failed wake''s messages moved to the pending recovery wake; pending wakes aren''t in the scan''s `state IN (''failed'',''delivered'')` filter), so the `total_changes` assertion passes even with `_wake_requeue_recorded` deleted. The aggregate exactly-4-`shell_busy`-events assertion is the real one-event-per-link guard — good — but consider an adoption-path double-pulse (a second delivered-unread wake adopting the same pending recovery) to make the dedupe branch itself red-able. Spec Verification''s Dedupe bullet is only substantively met by the aggregate count.

**Low 2 — nits, no action required.** `_wake_requeue_recorded` re-scans+json-parses all `wake.requeued` events per scanned row per 5s pulse (fine at sprint scale; json_extract keyed lookup if sprints grow long). `_busy_recovery_origin` raising on a malformed `busy:` key would wedge the whole reconcile loop (handcrafted keys only). No test pins a busy-chain wake failing non-SHELL_BUSY mid-chain (once-only stranding — conformant, unpinned).

Verified clean against spec #85 + the ratified reading: key-prefix counting is restart-safe (durable rows only; store-reconstruction test proves it); ordinals 2–5 with backoffs 15/60/180/300 and exhaustion at attempt 5 (index math checked); LIKE prefix can''t cross originals (`busy:12:` vs `busy:123:`); exactly one event per chain link with the classification extension; escalation notice carries shell + attempts + slot state, and `(orphan)` parsing matches the real broker detail (`conversation_launch.py:94-97`, `session_state` returns busy/orphan); broker untouched (diff = sprint_domain.py + 2 test files); no migration (`available_at` default keeps non-busy wakes immediately claimable); non-busy path semantics preserved; pause signaling outside the transaction in all three callers; armed-only reconcile switch holds.

Patch the Medium (planner may rule intended/spec-gap — then it''s a spec note) + re-push; thread closes when clean.', '2026-08-02 15:14:32', '2026-08-02 15:31:39', 'shell', '6d9dfa39a1fc4ee0a396d0cc27b1f46d');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (1250, 8, 9, 'sprint 86: unit 2: 0 major, 1 medium, 2 low — with DEV3 (msg #1249). Medium = SC-051 flag #139: resume-after-exhaustion re-pause trap; spec #85 silent on that edge, so a spec note may be the resolution if you rule the behavior intended. Not review-clean; Medium gates merge.', '2026-08-02 15:14:41', '2026-08-02 15:15:10', 'result', '4f126d354cd6405995a0b46153afe596');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (1251, 9, 5, 'SPRINT 86: RULING on REV2''s Medium (SC-051 / flag #139, msg #1249) — fix in PR #958, direction (b): human resume() after a wake_contention_exhausted pause is an EPISODE RESET. Re-deliver the stranded recovery wake (pending, available_at=now) as the human-sanctioned retry with a fresh contention budget; resume must not re-classify the exhausted chain''s stale durable evidence into an instant re-pause. Constraint: chain-length derivation must not count prior-episode rows against the new budget — distinguish episodes in the idempotency key or use the spec-permitted attempt-column migration, your call. Also fix resume() returning changed=True when the sprint ends paused. Spec #85 now carries this edge verbatim (Edge cases, last bullet) — build against the spec. REV2''s two Lows go to the report, no action. When green, request re-review from REV2 as usual; your merge still closes with the unit report, and close flag #139 with your merge (it''s your unit''s blocker).', '2026-08-02 15:16:18', '2026-08-02 15:31:39', 'task', '85a55ff093624e85861693618dc8dce1');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (1252, 5, 2, 'map gap: repo catalogue reports mapped branch feat/reopen-closed-chats while /home/j3d1/Repos/subfloor is on main and Sprint 86 work is on fix/shell-busy-wake-recovery — paths: .super-coder/scripts/sprint_domain.py, tests/test_sprint_recovery.py, tests/test_sprint_v2_domain.py. heal.', '2026-08-02 15:18:11', NULL, 'shell', '80523c07e153421893adc8df5dd74ce5');
